window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["audi/a8-d5"]={"a8-d5-acc-distance-setting-in-mmi":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Displays the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) distance setting on the MMI MIB2.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>13 – Auto Dist. Reg</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Distance basic setting option</strong>” or <em><strong>“Distance basic setting option”.</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose<strong>“On”</strong><strong> </strong>then confirm.</p>\n<p><em>The MMI needs to be restarted!</em></p>\n<p><em>Once the MMI has been restarted, go to Car/Driver Assistance/Audi Adaptive Cruise Control. You should see a new menu called “Basic setting”. Choose this option to set the distance level from 1 to 5 (each representing a “line”). Finally, once the setting has been made, push the ACC rod all the way in (towards the front of the car) so that it is completely deactivated. Replace it. This activates and deactivates ACC, and is necessary to recover the new setting.     </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/reglagesACCaudi-612d5092.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_7166-a399eb74.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-acc-driving-profile-selection-on-the-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the menu for manual selection of the Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) driving program on the MMI. Low/Standard/Dynamic driving program selection. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>13 – Regulation dist</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”<br/><br/> 5 – Choose byte<strong>“03</strong>”<br/>Then uncheck Bit<strong>“7</strong>”: “Drive-mode-selection,0-MMI-MMI menu ACC / 1 ride selection”.</p>\n<p><em>The MMI needs to be restarted!</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/reglagesACCaudi2-181c8b20.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-activate-a-second-phone-via-bluetooth":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to connect two phones simultaneously via Bluetooth to the MMI if you don’t have the Audi Phone Box option. <br/><br/><br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong><strong>Vehicle configuration – Support_second_phone</strong></strong>”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><em>Restart MMI</em></p>","a8-d5-activate-audi-traffic-jam-assist":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> activates Audi’s Traffic Jam Assist (TJA) (with vehicle equipped with Pre-Sense).  </p>\n<p>The Traffic Jam Assistant can take over steering at speeds of up to 65 km/h on well-maintained roads in the event of traffic jams. The system uses radar and ultrasonic sensors as well as the front camera to guide the vehicle by gently adjusting the steering and following the traffic ahead within the system’s limits. The traffic jam assistant uses road markings and other vehicles on the road to orientate itself.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/activation-Traffic-Jam-Assist-audi-1024x445-458f46ff.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Watch out! There are 4 lines of coding to do here.</strong>  (Use experimental data)</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> then click on  <strong>“<strong>13 –</strong> Auto Dist. Reg</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select<br/>Byte <strong>01</strong><br/>check Bit <strong>3</strong> “Traffic_jam_dependent_linear_tracking”<br/>check Bit <strong>4</strong> “Assistent_for_traffic_hold_up”<br/><br/>Byte <strong>02</strong> <br/>check Bit <strong>0</strong> “Automatic_driveaway_by_pretrigger”<br/>check Bit <strong>1</strong> “Automatic_driveaway_after_short_stop”<br/>check Bit <strong>2</strong> “Driveaway_by_triggerleaver”<br/>check Bit <strong>4</strong> “Curve_assistent”<br/><br/>Byte <strong>03</strong> <br/>Check Bit <strong>5</strong> “Traffic_jam_assistant_in_car_menu”.<br/><br/>Byte <strong>04</strong><br/>check Bit <strong>2</strong> “Emergency_Assist”<br/>check Bit <strong>7</strong> “Dense_traffic”<br/><br/>Byte <strong>06</strong> <br/>check Bit <strong>3</strong> “Emergency_steer_assist”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>A5 – Frt Sens. Drv</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/> 5 – Choose byte <strong>16</strong><br/>Then tick Bit <strong>5</strong> “STA”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“44 – Steering assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” and then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/> 5 – Select</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>02</strong><br/>check Bit <strong>0</strong> “Heading Control Assistant”.</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>06</strong><br/>check Bit <strong>0</strong> “Traffic Jam Guidance Assist”.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on <strong>“5F – Electronic Information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”<br/><br/> 5 – Select channels :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2 <strong>&gt;</strong> front_traffic_assist_0x41 <strong>&gt;</strong> activated</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2 <strong>&gt;</strong> front_traffic_assist_0x41_msg_bus <strong>&gt;</strong> terminal 15</li>\n</ul>","a8-d5-activate-automatic-gear-selection-in-virtual-cockpit":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Displays automatic speed selection in mode D and S on the virtual cockpit display.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>02 – Auto Trans</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Then select <strong>“Single Gear Display”</strong> from the drop-down list</p>\n<p><em>Set value to </em><strong><em>“D on/S on</em></strong></p>","a8-d5-activate-automatic-parking-brake":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the automatic parking brake function. When the vehicle is parked, the parking brake is automatically applied, so you no longer need to operate it manually.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>03 – Brake</strong></strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code “<strong>40168</strong>”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– Select Channel <em>: </em><em>“Frein de stationnement automatique</em>” or<em>“Automatische Parkbremse</em>”<em> </em>or<em> “Automatic parking brake”.</em><br/></p>\n<p>Set value to<strong>“Active</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/autoparkingbrakeaudi-3aa97785.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-activate-g-meter":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Adds the G-Meter (Accelerometer) to the Virtual Cockpit screen.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong> <br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“10</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“2</strong>”:<strong>“Display Acceleration</strong>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/accelerationdisplay-4bb736e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audi_a3_8v_power_torque-169cb34b.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-activate-hidden-mmi-menu":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the MMI’s hidden menu (Hidden Menu / Green Menu / Menu Engineering).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select<em><strong>“Developer test</strong> </em> <em><strong>mode</strong> </em><em>” </em>then activate.</p>\n<p><em>No need to restart the MMI.</em></p>\n<p><em>To open the hidden menu with NAV/MAP (or CAR) and RADIO. First press and hold NAV/MAP (or CAR), then press RADIO and wait 5 seconds. </em>.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/A4-Hidden-Menu-ec3628a6.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/A4-Hidden-Menu2-0030a834.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/access-the-audi-red-engineering-menu\">–&gt; To access the Audi Red Engineering menu</a></strong></p>","a8-d5-activate-lock-with-engine-running":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks the car while the engine is running. This is useful for warming up the car, for example, in complete safety.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>9</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p>Check Bit <strong>7</strong> “<em>central_locking_system_lock_unlock_at_engine_running”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/moteurlockaudi-1024x430-a815cb76.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>OBDeleven:</p>\n<p>Module 46 “Comfort System” Control Module <br/>Coding <br/>Search for ” <em>central_locking_system_lock_unlock_at_engine_running</em> ” <br/>The value is set to “Not Active” <br/>Change the value to “Active” <br/>Apply</p>","a8-d5-activate-mmi-cd-dvd-extraction":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the function for copying multimedia data (music, films, etc.), similar to the SD card function. Allows you to import/copy/load all compatible CD/DVD data onto the MMI PLUS hard disk (Jukebox).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select<em><strong>“Copy multimedia data</strong>” </em>/ “<em><strong>Multimediadaten kopieren-Optisches</strong> </em> Laufwerk<strong><em>Multimediadaten kopieren-Optisches Laufwerk</em></strong>” / “<strong><em>Multimedia Data-Optical Drive</em></strong>” then activate (set to <strong>1</strong>).</p>","a8-d5-activate-rs-monitor-on-mmi":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the RS Monitor on the MMI (MIB2+ MH2P or MIB3).  </p>\n<p><em>The RS monitor replaces the “Vehicle details” tab, but contains the same “Tilt angle display” as the first page.</em></p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>For</strong> <strong>MIB2+ MH2P :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>02</strong></p>\n<p>Bit <strong>4</strong> disabled <br/>Bit <strong>5</strong> enabled<br/>Bit <strong>6</strong> enabled<br/>Bit <strong>7</strong> disabled  </p>\n<p><em>Before applying the coding, check the “soft reset” box in the menu. <em><em>redémarrage à chaud / soft reset</em></em> ”  </em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>For</strong> <strong>MIB3 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>05</strong></p>\n<p>Bit <strong>0</strong> on<br/>Bit <strong>1</strong> off</p>\n<p><em>Before applying the coding, check the “soft reset” box in the menu. <em><em>redémarrage à chaud / soft reset</em></em> ”  </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rsmonitormlbevo-1024x768-6a34d36c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rsmonitormlbevo2-1024x768-f0353639.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rsmonitormlbevo3-1024x768-efb7b94a.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rsmonitormlbevo4-1024x768-54961ca1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rsmonitormlbevo5-1024x768-58867587.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-activate-trailer-coupling-retrofit":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the installation of a retrofit trailer hitch (trailer/towbar retrofit).  </p>\n<p><em>Caution! The configuration in the control unit for motor 01 is not supported for certain models. In this case, the coding can be skipped. Control units that are not installed can also be skipped. Please note that certain coding steps must be performed based on the part numbers of the installed components (camera).      </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Capture-decran-2024-01-09-215831-4f89678c.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Warning!! Depending on the modules you have installed, there are up to 12 coding lines to complete here; most ECUs require a long coding process with a “trailer” that must be enabled!  </strong><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1 </strong>– Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to<br/>the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2 </strong>– Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Select <strong>“Installation List”</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Check the box next to “<strong>69 – Trailer</strong>” in the list</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Save coding</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/trailergateway-3cb3c873.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“01 – Motor</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>05</strong>“<br/>. Then check bit “<strong>4</strong>“: “<strong>Trailer installed</strong>“</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/trailermoteur-fdaad0ca.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>13</strong>“<br/>Then check bit<strong> 4</strong> “Hitch_ecu”</p>\n<p><strong><em>If you have an electric vehicle: </em></strong> Set <strong>Bit 4</strong> of the “<strong>36</strong>” byte</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>14</strong>“<br/>Then check bit<strong> 6</strong> “Trailer monitoring”</p>\n<p><strong>Line 5:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>14</strong>“<br/>Then check bit<strong> 5</strong> “Trailer”<br/><br/><strong>Line 6:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>13 – Auto Dist. Reg. </strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>14117</strong>” or “<strong>20103</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click ” <strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then click “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte “<strong>03</strong>“<br/>Then set Bit<strong> 3</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/trailerdist-da789d91.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 7:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>74 – Chassis</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select the “<strong>00</strong>” byte<br/>Then set bit <strong>7</strong> (“trailer, 0 = not installed / 1 = installed”)<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 8:</strong></p>\n<p><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>3C – Lane Change</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select the “<strong>00</strong>” byte<br/>Then check bits <strong>4-5</strong> “10 with ECU for drawbar”<br/><br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 9:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>6C – Rearview Camera</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>04</strong>“<br/>Then set bit <strong>0</strong> (“equipment_ahk, installed”)<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 10:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>6D – Trunk Electrical System </strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>01</strong>“<br/>Then set bit <strong>7</strong> (“trailer, 0 = not installed / 1 = installed”)<br/><br/><strong>Line 11:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>A5 – Front, Sensors, Driver Assistance   </strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click ” <strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then click “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select the “<strong>11</strong>” byte</p>\n<p>Then set bit<strong> 0 ( </strong>“AAG, 0 = not_coded / 1 = coded”)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 12:</strong></p>\n<p><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>CF – Lane Change</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong></strong> 4 – Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong>,” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select the byte “<strong>00</strong>“<br/>Then check bits <strong>0-5</strong> “10 with ECU for drawbar”</p>\n<p><strong>Clear the error codes; if the Audi Pre Sense system still shows an error, restart the vehicle.</strong><br/></p>","a8-d5-activate-deactivate-daytime-running-lights-drl-with-mmi":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate/deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) from the MMI.  </p>\n<p>ATTENTION to your country’s regulations and technical inspection for daytime running lights!<br/>However, if you’re coding in your car to avoid using too much of your battery, this is a good solution…</p>\n<p><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>2</strong>, check bit <strong>1</strong> “drl_mmi”.</p>\n<p>OBDELEVEN: “DRL_MMI” active</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlmmiaudi-c12a3aa1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlmmiaudi2-c0f35d3d.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-audi-lane-assist-settings":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Adjusts the lane departure warning’s deactivation threshold for driver inactivity, the intensity of steering assistance, and the intensity of Audi Lane Assist steering wheel vibrations.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 (Steering assist intensity setting</strong>) <strong>:</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>A5 – Front camera</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code “<strong>20103</strong>”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– Select Channel <em>:</em> <em>“Lane Departure Warning Intensity Steering Assistance”</em> or</p>\n<p><em>“Spurhalteassistent Intensität Lenkunterstützung</em><br/></p>\n<p>Adjust value accordingly<br/><br/>Setting range:<br/><br/>– low (Lane Assist switches off earlier depending on ambient conditions, as less/more sensitive steering interventions are carried out)<br/>– medium (factory setting)<br/>– high (Lane Assist switches off later depending on ambient conditions, as more/more intensive steering interventions are carried out)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Driver inactivity deactivation threshold setting</strong>) <strong>:</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong> then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>A5 – Front camera</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code “<strong>20103</strong>”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– Select Channel <em>:</em><em>“Lane Departure Warning Deactivation Threshold Driver Inactivity</em>” or <em>“Spurhalteassistent Deaktivierungsschwelle Fahrerinaktivität”.</em><br/></p>\n<p>Adjust value accordingly<br/><br/>Setting range:<br/><br/>– early (deactivates Lane Assist within 7 seconds)<br/>– medium (factory setting, deactivates Lane Assist within 7 to 10 seconds)<br/>– late (deactivates Lane Assist within 11 to 15 seconds)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 (Steering vibration adjustment</strong>) <strong>:</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>A5 – Front camera</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code “<strong>20103</strong>”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– Choose Channel <em>:</em> “<strong>Directional stab. assist; intensity; steering wheel vibration </strong><em>“</em><br/></p>\n<p>Adjust value accordingly<br/><br/>Setting range:<br/><br/>– Low<br/>– Medium<br/>– High</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/audilaneassistvibration-1024x710-d5fcae97.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-audi-sound-system-volume-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to adjust the volume of the engine sound (Audi Sound System – Soundaktor) inside the car. To mute the sound, use value: 0.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”. <strong><strong><strong>A9 – Sound terminal structure</strong></strong></strong> ” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– Select Channel <em>:</em><strong>“Volume of structure borne noise actuator</strong>”.</p>\n<p>  Select your sound percentage (between 0 and 100)</p>","a8-d5-comfort-turn-signal":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>46 – Central Conv.</strong></strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Blinkzyklen</strong>” or “<strong>Cycles de clignotement</strong>” or “<strong>Turn Signal Control – Freeway flashing cycles</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose between<strong>“3</strong>” and<strong>“5</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/clignotantconfortaudi-1017x1024-8bdea6f1.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-configuring-automatic-locking-in-the-mmi":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates the menu entry for using the lock function when driving via the MMI.  </p>\n<p>By default, the vehicle locks the central locking system at speeds over 15 km/h, known as Auto Lock.</p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“46- Central Conv.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p>Select byte <strong>35</strong>: uncheck bit <strong>0</strong>“automatic_lock_not_at mmi”</p>\n<p><strong>OBDeleven</strong>:</p>\n<p>Select 209 automatic_lock_not_at mmi</p>\n<p>Set value to inactive</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/MMI_CAR_ZV-72acf6c5.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-daytime-running-light-deactivation-drl-with-handbrake-on":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to turn off the daytime running lights (DRL) using the parking brake (Park EPB).  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 09</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5 –</strong> Select byte <strong>2</strong> then set bit<strong> 2</strong><em> “drl_break,active”</em>.</p>","a8-d5-deactivate-automatic-activation-of-front-parking-aid":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable the automatic activation of the front parking assist (PDC)  </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>37</strong></p>\n<p>Set/clear bit <strong>1</strong> “auto_activation”<br/></p>","a8-d5-disable-am-frequency-on-the-mmi":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the AM radio frequency on the MMI (AM radio frequency is rarely used, unlike FM radio frequency).  </p>\n<p><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>14</strong></p>\n<p>Set bit <strong>1 “AM_disable”. </strong> </p>\n<figure>\n</figure>","a8-d5-disable-automatic-door-unlocking-with-dsg-in-p-mode":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Disables the feature that automatically unlocks all doors when the DSG automatic transmission is shifted to the “P” position.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1 –</strong> Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2 –</strong> Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on <strong>“Select”</strong> then click on <strong>” <strong>46 – Central Module Comfort System</strong> “</strong> .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Clear the bit  <strong>” </strong><strong>automatic_unlock_nar”</strong> </p>","a8-d5-disable-start-stop":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to disable Start and Stop operation.  </p>\n<p><em>Information: <em>Start/Stop</em> is inactive as long as the air-conditioning control is “on”. As soon as it is switched off, Start/Stop becomes active again. </em> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong><strong>08 </strong>– Air conditioning</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”<strong>.<br/></strong></p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Select “channel IDE03253 – A/C comfort parameter for on-off function”.</p>\n<p>base value: <strong>5 </strong><br/>replace with new value: <strong>0</strong></p>","a8-d5-display-intermediate-speeds-in-the-virtual-cockpit":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the intermediate km/h scale on the Virtual Cockpit speedometer. (Works only when the speedometer scale is set to km/h)   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>“, then on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>18</strong>“<br/>. Then check bit “<strong>1</strong>“: “<strong>Tachometer_erweiterte_Skalenteilung</strong>”  </p>\n<p>OBDeleven: Tachometer_advanced_scale_division -&gt; yes</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Tachometer_erweiterte_Skalenteilung-49c6acc8.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-easy-entry":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the “Easy Entry” function for the driver’s seat. By default, vehicles equipped with the electric steering column option automatically lock the driver’s seat when the vehicle is switched off and the driver’s door is open, to allow easy exit from the vehicle. In addition, when the car is unlocked and the driver’s door opened, the driver’s seat moves back to allow easy entry, and when the car is started, the seat moves forward to its last position. If you have a convenient/advanced key and driver memory seats, when you start the car, the seat moves to the recall memory stored on the key used to unlock the car (linked to button 1 or 2 of the driver seat memory buttons in the door trim). This modification enables this functionality when the electric steering column is not installed.      </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>09 – Central Electrics</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>14</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p>Check Bit <strong>2</strong> <em>“easy_entry_steering_column_via_mmi_configurable,active”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>36 – Seat Memory Driver</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>03</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p>Check Bit <strong>6</strong> <em>“Easy_Entry_front,0=not active / 1=active”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>06 – Seat Memory Passenger</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>03</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p>Check Bit <strong>6</strong> <em>“Easy_Entry_front,0=not active / 1=active”.</em><br/></p>\n<p>Restart the MMI!</p>\n<p>You should see the Easy Entry option under “Vehicle settings / Seats / Driver’s seat”. Make sure this option is checked. </p>","a8-d5-electric-tailgate-opening-delay-setting-with-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose: Allows you </strong>to adjust the activation time for the tailgate when you hold down the center button on the key fob and then release it to open the trunk. The default activation time/delay for opening/closing the trunk is 0.8 seconds (800 ms). You can increase the time it takes to open the trunk with the remote key. For example, if you accidentally open the trunk (because the key is in your pocket) when you didn’t intend to, you’ll have more time.    </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>46 – Central Conv</strong></strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select <strong>“Temps d’ouverture du coffre arrière avec télécommande”</strong> or<strong>“Actuation Time for opening rear lid with remote control</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6 – </strong> Select the value in ms<em> </em><br/><em>Default Value: 800 (ms)</em><br/><em>Range: 0 to 5,000 (ms)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/delaicoffreaudi-1024x997-4428f2ae.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-enable-automatic-window-lowering":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows the windows to be slightly ajar when the driver’s or passenger’s door is open. When a window is lowered, the cabin is no longer completely sealed, allowing the doors to be closed gently without having to slam them shut. (Windows Auto Drop)    <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 2 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“52 – Passenger door</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>3</strong>“<br/>. Then uncheck bit “<strong>1</strong>“: “<strong>short_drop,active</strong>“<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>42 – Driver’s Door</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte “<strong>3</strong>“<br/>. Then uncheck bit “<strong>1</strong>“: “<strong>short_drop,active</strong>“</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Window_Auto_Drop_Audi-1024x333-72c26167.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-enable-the-recirculation-memory-function":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the “recirculation” setting memory. If you have enabled it, it will remain active the next time the vehicle is started. Please note that your Audi has an automatic recirculation function via the MMI system; when this is enabled, the recirculation indicator light does not illuminate while the function is active.    </p>\n<p> <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“08 – Climatronic</strong>” /<strong>“08 – Auto HVAC</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5 –</strong> At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>IDE01476 – Store air recirculation setting with terminal 15 off</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>Storing</strong>” or “<strong>Save</strong>,” then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Air_Recirculation_Memory_audi-1024x364-ddea2ff5.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-heated-seat-settings":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Used to adjust the seat heating temperature, you can increase or decrease the heating level of all or part of the seat by up to 5 degrees Celsius to obtain the optimum temperature setting for you.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Fine adjustment of seat heating level 1</strong>” or “Sitzheizung Feineinstellung Stufe 1”.</p>\n<p>Then levels <strong>2</strong> and <strong>3</strong> <em>(Heated seat power)</em><br/><br/> 6 – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>Here, select the range of values: -5 to +5 (degrees Celsius) relative to the base temperature, then confirm.</p>","a8-d5-heated-steering-wheel-settings":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to adjust the temperature of the steering wheel heater, you can increase or decrease the heating level of all or part of the seat by up to 5 degrees Celsius to obtain the optimum temperature setting for you.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“16 – Steering Column Electronics</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Steering wheel heating Temperature 1</strong>” or<strong>“Chauffage du volant température</strong><strong>1</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Then temperatures <strong>2</strong> and <strong>3</strong> <em>(Heated flywheel power)</em><br/><br/> 6 – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom of the page.<br/>On this menu, select the range of values: -5 to +5 (degrees Celsius) relative to the base temperature, then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/volantchauffantaudi-1024x686-9db652c7.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-lap-timer":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add the stopwatch to the ODB/Virtual Cockpit.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>” .<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“3</strong>”:<strong>“Lap Timer active</strong>”.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/GOLF-7-VAGCOM---CHECK-DES-AIGUILLES-1-dab4b41b.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-lock-unlock-confirmation-beeps":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables vehicle lock/unlock confirmation with beeps.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte <strong>4</strong>: </em> </p>\n<p>Check Bit <strong>6</strong><em>“Horn_acknowledgement”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/beepaudi-1024x405-74a8cc27.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Modify number of beeps on closing (none/single/double)):</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel</strong>: </em><em>“sounder_settings-beeptime_closing_central_locking</em>”.</p>\n<p><em>Adjust value </em>:<br/>default: double_beep (2x acknowledgement tone)<br/>single_beep (1x acknowledgement tone)<br/>no_beep (no acknowledgement tone on locking)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 (Change the number of beeps when opening (none/single/double)):</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel</strong>: </em><em>“sounder_settings-beeptime_opening_central_locking</em>”.</p>\n<p><em>Adjust value </em>:<br/>default: no_beep (no acknowledgement tone on unlocking)<br/>single_beep (1x acknowledgement tone)<br/>double_beep (2x acknowledgement tone)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/beepsettingaudi-1013x1024-b6ef3ffb.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 4 ( <strong>Unlocking</strong> beep</strong>) <strong>:</strong><br/></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>46 – Central Conv</strong></strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>central_locking_system-beep_at_opening</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>On</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/beepunlockaudi-1024x699-a8a10409.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-locking-unlocking-confirmation-flashing-lights":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows you to change the vehicle lock/unlock confirmation with the number of indicators.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong><strong>Line 1<strong>(For number of flashers on lock</strong>) :</strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>46 – Central Conv</strong></strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Turn Signal control-Confirmation flashing locking central locking; flashing cycles</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6 </strong>– On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose :</p>\n<p><em>“1” (single flash)</em><br/><em>“2” (double flash)</em></p>\n<p>then click “Submit.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/clignotantlockaudi-1024x704-0ed79909.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 <strong><strong>(<strong>For number of flashers on unlocking</strong></strong>)</strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong><strong>46 – Central Conv</strong></strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Turn Signal control-Confirmation flashing unlocking central locking; flashing cycles</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose :</p>\n<p><em>“0” (no flashing)<br/></em><em>“1” (single flash)</em><br/><em>“2” (double flash)</em></p>\n<p>then click “Submit.”</p>","a8-d5-needle-check":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the scanning of the speedometer needles when the car is started. (Works with Virtual Cockpit) (Needle Sweep)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select byte<strong>“1</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“0</strong>”:<strong>“Gauge Test/Needle Sweep (Stading) active</strong>” or “Staging”.<br/></p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/GOLF-7-VAGCOM---CHECK-DES-AIGUILLES-1-dab4b41b.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-panel-display-in-virtual-cockpit":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> displays speed limit signs in the Virtual Cockpit (Sign Assist).   <br/><br/><br/>The vehicle must be equipped with Lane Assist.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 8 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1 </strong>– Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to<br/>the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2 </strong>– Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule function list BAP-traffic_sign_recognition_0x21</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose<strong>“activated</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule function list BAP-traffic_sign_recognition_0x21_msg-bus</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Data Extended</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6 – </strong>On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_road_sign_identification</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose<strong>“activated</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6 – </strong>On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_road_sign_identification_over_threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose<strong>“activated</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 5:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>A5 – Frt Sens. Drv.  Assist</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5 </strong>– Select byte<strong>“58</strong>”<br/>Then, in the Bit <strong>6-7</strong> drop-down menu, select<strong>“40 VZE_traffic_sign_recognition,installed</strong>”.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 6 <strong>(Optional)</strong>:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>A5 – Frt Sens. Drv.  Assist</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Display end of speed limit symbol</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose<strong>“activated</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 7 (optional) :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on “.<strong>A5 – Frt Sens. Drv.  Assist</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Display valid additional characters</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose<strong>“activated</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 8:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte<strong>“5</strong>”<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“2</strong>”:<strong>“Traffic Sign Recognition installed</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Select byte<strong>“14</strong>”<br/>Then check bit<strong>“6</strong>”:<strong>“traffic_sign_detection</strong>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/panneauaudi-8a53d2c3.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-rear-lights-activated-with-daytime-running-lights-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rear lights to turn on when the daytime running lights (Scandinavian DRL) are activated. <br/><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>2</strong>, set bit <strong>3 ” </strong>sl_at_drl”</p>\n<p>OBDELEVEN: “SL_AT_DRL” is enabled</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlaudi-f9e7108c.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-reprogram-a-new-battery":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to reprogram or recode all data for the new battery after it has been replaced. <br/><br/><br/><strong>Watch out! There are 4 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click ” <strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Adaptation—Nominal Battery Capacity</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the rated capacity listed on your battery. For example: “<strong>70Ah</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Adaptation—Battery Technology</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu further down<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the corresponding value<br/>. For example: For the VARTA E39, select “<strong>Etoffe</strong>” / “<strong>Fleece</strong>” for AGM.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Adaptation—Battery Manufacturer</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu further down the page<br/>.<br/>From this menu, select the corresponding brand:<br/>For example: For the VARTA E39, select “<strong>VAO</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>Line 4:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>19 – CAN Gateway</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Battery Configuration—Battery Serial Number</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>.<br/>In this menu, enter the corresponding serial number:<br/>Note: Enter only the <strong>last 10 digits</strong> of the serial number.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>Battery Status Detection Features:</strong></p>\n<p><br/>The battery status detection in the battery data module calculates the following values, which are transmitted via the LIN bus to the J533 diagnostic data bus interface:<br/>1 “battery not present” detection: if the battery data module does not detect a battery for<br/>more than 30 seconds, a corresponding bit is set to 1<br/>2 voltage that temporarily allows for optimal battery charging<br/>3 “engine start capability” bit. It indicates whether the battery is currently capable of starting<br/>the engine or not<br/>4. The amount of charge that can still be temporarily drawn from the battery before reaching the limit of<br/>its ability to start the engine<br/>5. The battery’s current state of charge<br/>6. Battery aging. Battery aging can be determined using parameters such a<br/>, including the battery’s energy storage capacity and instantaneous power output.<br/>7 battery open-circuit voltage<br/>8 battery internal resistance  </p>\n<p><strong>The battery sensor in the J367 battery monitoring control unit:</strong></p>\n<p>Knowing whether the battery has enough electrical energy to restart the engine is essential for the start-stop system to function properly.<br/>The control module is located directly on the “negative” terminal of the ground wire and is connected to the diagnostic interface via the LIN data bus.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/charge-batterie-c76863ff.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Signal Usage:</strong><br/>The battery sensor records the following values:<br/>– Battery temperature<br/>– Battery voltage<br/>– Charging current<br/>The battery temperature is calculated using a lookup table and the ambient temperature.<br/>It also allows for estimates of the battery’s charging time.<br/>Using the data obtained in this way, it is possible to adjust the charging control—particularly the charging voltage—to the battery’s state of charge and operating conditions. The goal is to increase the availability of the start-stop system by optimally utilizing data from the starter battery. </p>\n<p><strong>Consequences in the Event of a Malfunction</strong><br/>If the battery sensor is defective, the battery status can no longer be detected correctly.<br/>A fault is logged in the diagnostic interface’s fault memory. The start-stop system is deactivated. </p>\n<p><strong>Battery</strong></p>\n<p>The vehicle’s battery is housed in the engine compartment and protected by a battery tray. The size and type of battery depend on the engine version, equipment, and country-specific variant. Standard batteries, EFB batteries, and AGM batteries are used.<br/>Vehicles with gasoline engines and start/stop systems are equipped with an EFB battery, while vehicles with diesel engines and start/stop systems are equipped with an AGM battery. Vehicles with auxiliary heaters typically have an AGM battery.   </p>\n<p><strong>EFB</strong></p>\n<p>An EFB battery (short for Enhanced Flooded Battery) is a reinforced flooded battery. The positive plate inside the battery is coated with an additional layer of polyester mesh. This provides the battery’s active material with additional support on the plate. These batteries have greater resistance to charge-discharge cycles than standard batteries. During charging, an EFB battery is treated like a standard battery.    </p>\n<p><strong>AGM Battery</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-agm-f4b81a74.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In AGM (Absorbent Glass Mat) batteries, the battery electrolyte is retained within a microporous glass mat. An AGM battery is characterized not only by even greater resistance to charge-discharge cycles compared to an EFB battery, but also by its leak-proof design. When charging, follow the charger’s user manual and, if applicable, select the AGM battery program.  </p>\n<p>In the case of AGM batteries, the automotive battery electrolyte is retained within a microporous glass mat. In addition to<br/>increased resistance to charge-discharge cycles, an AGM battery is characterized by its high level of leak resistance. Sealing is of crucial<br/>importance, particularly when the battery is installed in<br/>the passenger compartment. When charging, follow the charger’s user manual and, if necessary, select the program for<br/>AGM batteries.   </p>\n<p>Below, we can see the brand, serial number, and manufacturer of the battery</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/batterie-124711ff.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-speed-of-radar-deactivation-or-reversing-camera":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Selects the speed at which the radar and/or reversing camera are deactivated.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Switch-off speed for parking assist</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose a value between<strong>“0</strong>” and<strong>“15</strong>” km/h, depending on your preference.</p>","a8-d5-suppress-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to suppress the audible alarm and warning light in the Virtual Cockpit when driving without a seatbelt.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>0</strong>:<br/>Bit <strong>2-4</strong>: select <strong>“Seat Belt Warning inactive”</strong> from the drop-down list.</p>\n<p><strong><em>OR</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose <strong>“Deactivate</strong> <strong>Seat belt warning”</strong> / <strong>“</strong> <strong>Désactiver l’avertissement de ceinture”.</strong> <br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Oui</strong>” /<strong>“Yes”</strong> and confirm.</p>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/8U0_920_940_Module17_Adaptation_desactivate_seat_b-77d3b532.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","a8-d5-suppress-electric-tailgate-beeps":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to deactivate beeps when opening/closing the trunk/electric liftgate.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>  6D – Elect. Trunk” </strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then type in the code<strong>“12345</strong>”<br/><br/> 5 – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/> 6 – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“ENG131232-MAS01911 – Ausstattungen aktivieren-Tongeber</strong>” /<strong>“activate equipment sound generator</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“not</strong> <strong>active</strong>” and confirm.</p>","a8-d5-unlock-the-menus-while-driving":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven Audi A8 D5 4N\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/AUDI-A8-4N-f34770f5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to unlock certain multimedia system menus while driving, and to enable text entry for CarPlay and Android Auto, which are normally disabled when the vehicle is in motion.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 (Menu)</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Locked menu contents</strong>” <strong>(FB <strong>CAR, media </strong>, and nav)</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>non_blocked</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>NHSTA Properties</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>not_activated</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 (CarPlay)</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select “<strong>nhtsa_limitation_switches_for_carplay_no_softKeyboard</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu further down<br/>the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>not_activated</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 4 (Android Auto)</strong><br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, select “<strong>nhtsa_limitation_switches_for_androidauto_no_text_input</strong>“<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu located toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>not_activated</strong>” and then confirm.</p>","a8-d5-ventilated-seat-settings":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to fine-tune seat ventilation, you can increase or decrease all respective seat ventilation levels by up to 10% compared to factory delivery to obtain the optimum amount of ventilation for you.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 (Front seats):</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Fine adjustment of seat ventilation level 1</strong>” or “Sitzlüftung Feineinstellung Stufe 1”.</p>\n<p>Then levels <strong>2</strong> and <strong>3</strong> <em>(Power of ventilated seats)</em><br/><br/> 6 – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu, but towards the bottom of the page.<br/>On this, choose the range of values: -10 to +10 (% – per cent) in relation to the basic ventilation speed, then validate.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Rear seats):</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/> 4 – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/> 5 – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Fine adjustment of rear seat ventilation level 1</strong>” or “Sitzlüftung hinten Feineinstellung Stufe 1”.</p>\n<p>Then levels <strong>2</strong> and <strong>3</strong> <em>(Power of <em>ventilated</em> seats)</em><br/><br/> 6 – On this same page there is a second drop-down menu, but towards the bottom of the page.<br/>On this, choose the range of values: -10 to +10 (% – per cent) in relation to the base ventilation speed, then validate.</p>","a8-d5-wireless-carplay-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Enables Apple CarPlay Wireless and Google Android Auto Wireless to be activated without the need for a USB cable.  </p>\n<p><em><em>The vehicle must have an enabled USB wired CarPlay connection (Audi Smartphone Interface) and a MIB2 Plus with MH2p system must be </em>running firmware P2470 or higher (MH2p_ER_AUG35_P2470) or MIB3<em>.</em> </em><br/><em>Before you start, disassociate/delete all Apple devices from CarPlay and Bluetooth (including deleting the car if already paired from the Apple device itself – settings/general/CarPlay).</em></p>\n<p><strong>Watch out! There are 7 lines of coding to do here. </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1 (Wifi):</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Choose Channel <em>:</em> <em>“</em>Vehicle configuration – wlan_5ghz_switch<em>“.</em></p>\n<p><em>Set value to “ON</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Wifi):</strong><br/><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Choisir Canal <em>:</em> <em>“</em>Véhicule configuration – WiFi_Client_HMI<em>“</em></p>\n<p><em>Set value to “ON</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 (Apple Carplay):</strong><br/><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Choose Channel <em>:</em> <em>“Vehicle configuration – Apple_DIO_Wireless”.</em></p>\n<p><em><em>Set value to “ON</em></em></p>\n<p>Line 4 (Apple Carplay):<br/><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” Select ” then click on “Select”.5F – Information Electr.” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Choose Channel <em>:</em> <em>“Vehicle configuration – Apple_DIO”.</em></p>\n<p><em><em>Set value to “ON</em></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 5 (Android Auto):</strong><br/><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select Channel <em>:</em> <em>“</em>Vehicle configuration – Google_GAL_Wireless<em>“.</em></p>\n<p><em><em>Set value to “ON</em></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 6 (Android Auto):</strong><br/><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Choose Channel <em>:</em> <em>“</em>Vehicle configuration – Google_GAL<em>“.</em></p>\n<p><em><em>Set value to “ON</em></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 7 (Android Auto):</strong><br/><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” then click on “Select”.<strong><strong>5F – Information Electr.</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select Channel <em>:</em> <em>“</em>Vehicle configuration – MirrorLink<em>“.</em></p>\n<p><em><em>Set value to “ON</em></em></p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Restart <strong>MIB3</strong>, reset MMI (hold down volume control for at least 10-15 seconds)</p>\n<p><em>Don’t plug your Apple device into the USB port!</em></p>\n<p>Make sure the WIFI access point is enabled in the MMI settings.<br/>On your iPhone under Settings -&gt; Wi-Fi, your car should appear with ***_5GHZ. <br/>Pair your Apple device with Bluetooth, it should now ask you if you want to activate CarPlay.<br/>If not, delete the pairing, first connect to the car’s Wi-Fi from the Apple device, then retry pairing via Bluetooth.</p>"};
